9-6486-5860-947e-ec390bfd044a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77715/selection/502c57970a47bcabacf1f97effbbcf3d719c848b1763e0dd7a05956da566de95" :answer-field/choices ["q-77715/selection/7e16d6340874a14e1977dee7ec33ecc777485165853357dbc59709f189dddbc5" "q-77715/selection/f8a17dfa9c6c617e6d9a878baa76f0037adffd2fc9e54a73d00cc44b53836b76" "q-77715/selection/4231723aadc03b6839863a5e98ff606f388500b70dcc96c6e4b31deac8087bcc" "q-77715/selection/86b305451e38df0bb7aba2e2c7b4471e73f2f1c8b0267c9b4c2b46ed044160fd" "q-77715/selection/502c57970a47bcabacf1f97effbbcf3d719c848b1763e0dd7a05956da566de95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77715" :question/id #uuid "52bcce79-5f5b-5440-80f7-1cea6e680e2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-77715" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/0b56d6a20b6a3e01dafa9770eb328ebaab5c14f76d87026c160c9be0d8926e74.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}},$ the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(-3,7)$ and ${B}^{′}(6,2),$ as shown below.\n\n!