 by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}},$ the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(-3,6)$ and ${B}^{′}(5,-3),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/26d4f8e966818e27a0858da0aa8757cf71ebbd1ef0e0544a2b8a126810252def.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77709/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77709"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77717/selection/ada70ebc2fa586a6dfd3bc00629d62625680cb8c8dc05a0282efaf285d7667de" :answer/id #uuid "e2303282-ee20-5386-b345-0758948c3876" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/19dc7b72e149547ff51758dadf84f94be080a68227239e07239ce0659ade5a5a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77717/selection/683a402fa0b0e3acac4b3bed4e91e6a56f263c0fc1f153ce9fcd075866add312" :answer/id #uuid "1a0c3e8d-61f0-5ce0-afcc-4e8ec9c4eb64" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad