1cdeac2fdb9a228fb7fd022078201147da9ee2c59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77717" :question/id #uuid "f9161e73-0db0-599d-b045-fa10e5d3039c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77717" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/fc7bebddc280debd4bde32393cabfa4a6a91a782d38e5406f374cc4eaa4ac68f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}},$ the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ 7 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(5,7)$ and ${B}^{′}(-9,-3),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/177ca7f40ef24cf2f45a15b78487700d1f0efd094c975079cf4704b46debefb1.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77717/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77717"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281556/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "df433510-1919-54ee-994a-7b458d1ec5fb" :answer/type :an