56/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "76030edb-e3bc-5027-b7e7-0a0e21276d83" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281556/field-4/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-281556/field-4/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281556" :question/id #uuid "6affb64c-3824-5cb5-981e-e31c13ef29ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-281556" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ has endpoints at $Y(2,-2)$ and $Z(0,1).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints $\\overset{―}{{Y}^{′}{Z}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${Y}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,$ and $\\,{Z}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{YZ}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${Y}^{′}(4,-4)$ and ${Z}^{′}(0,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-281556/field-1" "q-281556/field-2" "q-281556/field-3" "q-281556/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-12031"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/205badcabf4c2444f7ca8b38e189b1a0f8957e324ba7fb1a28909dc4afdd8c75.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(2,-3),(-2,1),(2,3)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4e456209fc818f606bfe83324b05843b0122840161a84a8d729927f4050f2397.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-159801/selection/701b72cad87674f7c550c11bffb0bc73dd269167f17c62044d95297b76191013" :answer/id #uuid "869f085e-90c3-5d5b-8228-6ebeabbf0ef0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/98150e2e7b7cb55643f588b885c3f57a34da186834dcbebd2cb7b35151317519.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159801/selection/1928cc0fbb195768af381de0ef5afd9d42595b046de157b5e23be8e697b58fdf" :answer/id #uuid "e6f322ad-95a5-5c05-b401-86954c9727d9" :answer/t