 $PQR$ has vertices at $P(-2,2),\\,Q(2,3),$ and $R(0,-2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$, the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${P}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Q}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{R}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 18 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$ are ${P}^{′}(2,2),$\n${Q}^{′}(18,8),$ ${R}^{′}(-8,-4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-281566/field-1" "q-281566/field-2" "q-281566/field-3" "q-281566/field-4" "q-281566/field-5" "q-281566/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8093/selection/cd0e6a71941ff4ab5453ef2405897ef9300acaeaed06097f030f5a085f63bbcf" :answer/id #uuid "2355d133-5dbb-5e81-999a-17dcdb59efcc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4672e5a5e616c8c6f4d40d1f29a2a8794da4e8d61c8bab09b7483ec292a91410.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8093/selection/27a6151f9501c4b219ee49c0a45c0ea9e2a5f478e0cba0ad8df81dcff2aea35b" :answer/id #uuid "5a50a9e7-7fae-5138-a59d-bc35b4e16167" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/0f5bf56cb4e4546079d89fd97b9533676116d4cff5435cbc926b925af5d3f637.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8093/selection/3e96b14328071392c21b5babb999410c98ed8fc17e9446d1b5288a3c46af816c" :answer/id #uuid "8b324a91-bea2-54b7-bd10-b62fe9522711" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/3caf43c4c62614f0c38b2f32c12892820ab4ae732669767b0d50104c85eee605.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8093/selection/ce930bd296918c6f8be3ec8404e98fe3745cc7aeca84c2b6277f1f49b82e9cd6" :answer/id #uuid "dd26178c-0f39-577c-bcc1-6694ee358588" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/cb590309256b4836583132f707ceb405472d104908f5df45a0d41dfa18c84a30.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8093/selection/d733c81d2f53083c81c0cfaabaf5d5a504882e7de843000c16dc881d555e4226" :answer/id #uuid "de241fd6-65ee-552b-983c-e4fdb893b863" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/54496f08a7d4d6b5d37713ffe6d4bc903d48da90def0b273c114fb3b27e32bc9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8093/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33598e84-2446-5510-8a29-1f659efdd00e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8093/selection/3e96b14328071392c21b5babb999410c98ed8fc17e9446d1b5288a3c46af816c" :answer-field/choices ["q-8093/selection/cd0e6a71941ff4ab5453ef2405897ef9300acaeaed06097f030f5a085f63bbcf" "q-8093/selection/27a6151f9501c4b219ee49c0a45c0ea9e2a5f478e0cba0ad8df81dcff2aea35b" "q-8093/selection/3e96b14328071392c21b5babb999410c98ed8fc17e9446d1b5288a3c46af816c" "q-8093/selection/ce930bd296918c6f8be3ec8404e98fe3745cc7aeca84c2b6277f1f49b82e9cd6" "q-8093/selection/d733c81d2f53083c81c0cfaabaf5d5a504882e7de843000c16dc881d555e4226"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8093" :question/id #uuid "620f4a44-3dbc-5f00-8f93-44670447e38b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8093" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/369dde2e95b52356b71972b8f1103430e0a840d3d0478626dc5a78cba0f51a41.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $ABCD$ is shown above. Which of the following is ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′},$ the image of $ABCD$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}$ are $(-1,3),(0,6),(0,8),(-1,5)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/3caf43c4c62614f0c38b2f32c12892820ab4ae732669767b0d50104c85eee605.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-8093/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8093"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281563/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c65cbb20-03de-5881-acd6-1313c469fc34" :answer/type :answer.type/mat